{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>YHWH from Sinai came.</b> One may say: the Holy One, blessed be He — it is He who comes from Sinai and shines, as in the model of 'May YHWH bless you from Zion.'" "<b>And He shone from Seir to them.</b> From the direction of Seir the beginning of the shining of the lightning-flashes and torches was seen. And the reason it uses the expression 'and He shone' is because Mount Seir is to the east of Sinai. <b>He appeared from Mount Paran.</b> Mount Paran too is to the east of Sinai. And the reason the Holy One, blessed be He, traveled from the east of the world was for the honor of Israel — to go to meet them, for they always travel from west to east, as Rashi explained in the portion of Masei." "<b>From His right hand, fire of law to them.</b> Because the right hand is the way of affection, as it is written: 'and His right hand embraced me.'" "<b>Ashdat.</b> It is written as one word and read as two."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:20.810330757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}